1
00:00:02,235 --> 00:00:04,375
(Sheldon:)Two one six four two zero

2
00:00:04,372 --> 00:00:06,402
(Sheldon:)one nine eight nine.

3
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:10,107
(Sheldon:)And that, little lady,
is pi to a thousand places.

4
00:00:10,111 --> 00:00:12,111
(Amy:)I'd say I'm sorry I asked,

5
00:00:12,113 --> 00:00:14,483
(Amy:)except I didn't.

6
00:00:14,482 --> 00:00:16,882
(Sheldon:)Oh, look, it's the
Scientific American

7
00:00:16,884 --> 00:00:19,654
(Sheldon:)that covered the paper
Leonard and I wrote.

8
00:00:19,653 --> 00:00:21,623
(Amy:)Oh, let me see.

9
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:24,222
(Sheldon:)I have mixed feelings
about doing interviews.

10
00:00:24,225 --> 00:00:26,425
(Sheldon:)I like the part where I talk.

11
00:00:26,427 --> 00:00:29,967
(Sheldon:)I do not like the part
where the other man talks.

12
00:00:31,498 --> 00:00:34,438
(Amy:)Sheldon, this article doesn't
mention Leonard at all.

13
00:00:34,435 --> 00:00:36,205
(Sheldon:)Well, that
can't be right.

14
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:39,173
(Amy:)It only refers to
"Dr. Cooper and his team."

15
00:00:39,173 --> 00:00:41,103
(Amy:)Did you even talk about him?

16
00:00:41,108 --> 00:00:43,708
(Sheldon:)All I did was answer a few
questions about the theory.

17
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:45,841
(Sheldon:)And then expressed my gratitude
that Scientific American

18
00:00:45,846 --> 00:00:49,286
(Sheldon:)doesn't include any of those
smelly perfume cards.

19
00:00:49,283 --> 00:00:51,983
(Amy:)Poor Leonard.

20
00:00:51,986 --> 00:00:54,386
(Sheldon:)Why? The theory
he came up with

21
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:55,918
(Sheldon:)just got mentioned in
Scientific American.

22
00:00:55,923 --> 00:00:57,293
(Sheldon:)He ought to be thrilled.

23
00:00:57,291 --> 00:00:58,721
(Amy:)He might not be.

24
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:00,796
(Sheldon:)Oh, maybe you're right.

25
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:03,165
(Sheldon:)He is kind of a lump.

26
00:01:03,164 --> 00:01:04,364
(Amy:)Think about it.

27
00:01:04,365 --> 00:01:06,265
(Amy:)How would you feel
if you were referred to

28
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:07,937
(Amy:)as part of Leonard's team?

29
00:01:07,935 --> 00:01:10,305
(Sheldon:)Oh, I'd be incensed.

30
00:01:10,304 --> 00:01:12,734
(Amy:)So you see what
I'm getting at?

31
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:15,270
(Sheldon:)Squeaky wheel
gets the grease?

32
00:01:15,276 --> 00:01:16,676
(Sheldon:)No.

33
00:01:16,677 --> 00:01:18,607
(Sheldon:)Grass is always greener?

34
00:01:18,612 --> 00:01:20,312
(Amy:)Try again.

35
00:01:20,314 --> 00:01:21,984
(Sheldon:)Well, I don't know--
we're all Groot?

36
00:01:21,982 --> 00:01:24,082
(Sheldon:)Just tell me.

37
00:01:24,085 --> 00:01:26,155
(Amy:)Leonard is as much
a part of this paper

38
00:01:26,153 --> 00:01:28,183
(Amy:)as you are,
and he was overlooked.

39
00:01:28,189 --> 00:01:30,189
(Amy:)He's going to feel bad.

40
00:01:30,191 --> 00:01:32,461
(Sheldon:)But it wasn't my fault.

41
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:33,990
(Sheldon:)I didn't exclude him.

42
00:01:33,994 --> 00:01:35,624
(Sheldon:)And I didn't write the article.

43
00:01:35,629 --> 00:01:38,729
(Amy:)Remember that time you didn't
get picked to pull the sword out

44
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:41,902
(Amy:)of the stone at Disneyland and
they let that other kid do it?

45
00:01:41,902 --> 00:01:43,972
Oh, that kid!

46
00:01:46,906 --> 00:01:50,306
(Amy:)Poor Leonard.

47
00:01:50,311 --> 00:01:52,141
(Amy:)Exactly.

48
00:01:52,146 --> 00:01:54,616
(Sheldon:)For the record,
that kid was a terrible choice.

49
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:56,385
(Sheldon:)If you cry when you drop
your churro,

50
00:01:56,383 --> 00:01:58,783
(Sheldon:)you do not have what it takes
to rule England.

51
00:02:00,253 --> 00:02:03,923
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

